questions.explanation:
Birth rate $=\frac{\Delta \mathrm{N}}{\mathrm{N} \Delta \mathrm{t}}$

Here, $ N=250 $\begin{aligned} \Delta \mathrm{t} & =1 \text { year } \\\\ \Delta \mathrm{N} & =2500-250 \\\\ & =2250 \end{aligned} 

 \begin{aligned} \text { Birth rate } & =\frac{2250}{250 \times 1} \\\\ & =9 \end{aligned}

